Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||02-21-2001||07:47 PM||||If I'm not mistaken I think the Haynes book says my 86 GT fuel tank should hold just a little over 10 gallons. Just ran out of gas as I coasted into an station and all I could get into the tank was 9.1. What gives? Ok, I just pumped until the station nozzle kicked off but is it possible to coax a full gallon in after the pump kicks off.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000001||SteveJ||02-21-2001||07:59 PM||||Around here the pump clicks off at 13 gallons for a 10 gallon tank. Count your self lucky. ||||reg||12
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||02-21-2001||08:05 PM||||Yeh, I saw that on 20/20. They have the same problem in LA. I guess it just takes more revenue to cover ordinary business expenses in the big city. BTW how many times has your car been stolen.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||02-21-2001||10:18 PM||||I thought the earlyier cars had like a 10 gal-ish tank.  I know on my 87 has an 11.7 gal tank.  The 85-86 have one size tank and the 87-88 have a larger tank.  I know this wasn't that much help but for what it's worth.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||02-21-2001||10:38 PM||||I have always wondered about Fiero gas tanks.  I sputtered into the gas station the other day and I could only get 10.8 gallons in there and its supposed to hold 11.9.  I have heard this from just about every Fiero owner I have every talked to.  When warmer weather comes I am going to change my fuel pump so I will take a look at the tank.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||Feenx||02-22-2001||01:58 AM||||the 85 owners manual states<BR>that the fuel tank holds 10.3 gal.<BR>or 38.6 liters..if you happin to live in <BR>Canada like me..lol<BR>I think 84 to 86 uses the same size tank.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>86 Sport Coupe (Red)<BR>2.5L Auto||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elenor84||02-22-2001||03:36 AM||||Hey guys, I drive a 84 2m4 and it has a 30 litre tank(I"m canadian)...whatever that converts to...thats the 84's<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||02-22-2001||10:03 AM||||My owners manual for an 86GT says 10.3 gallons.  I've never been able to put over about 9.4 in it and that's topping it off.  There was still fuel in the tank sloshing around when I ran out of gas once.  I left my key on and sloshed it around to pump the presure up to get me a few more blocks to the station. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||02-22-2001||08:32 PM||||You need to consider how the fuel is drawn up through the fuel pump.  I don't have a clue as to what the pickup strainer looks like, but if it is not at the bottom of the tank, you'll run out of gas before the tank is dry. After fuel pump replacement, my car still took less than 10 gallons to fill an empty tank..<P>Haynes manual say 84's had a 10.5 gal tank and 85-86 had a 10.3 gal tank.  I think that is incorrect.  The 84s had the smallest tank size (I thought 8.5 gal).  You can't use an 85-88 tank in an 84 car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DavidHenshaw||02-22-2001||10:11 PM||||I think Old Lar has the right idea. These tanks are long and flat and it looks like the fuel pump can't get all the fuel out. I know my car was cutting in and out as I was rounding corners, starting stoping etc.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
